/***
# iterator

An **iterator** is a lazy sequence: it yields the entries (key, value) of an
iterable as it is iterated — `for k, v in it`, `collect(it)` —, computing
each on demand. `map`, `filter`, `keys`, `values`, `zip` give iterators.

## Constructors

`iterator(it)` iterates any iterable (an array, a dict, a str, a range, …):
the type constructor form of `iterate`.

@snippet constructors

## See also

- [Functional](../functional.md) (`map`, `filter`, `reduce`),
  [comprehensions](../comprehensions.md).

@type iterator
***/

example constructors {
    [collect(iterator([1, 2])), collect(iterator({a: 1})), isIterator(iterator([]))]
    = [[1, 2], [1], true]
}
